      <article class="page" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/CreativeWork">
        <meta itemprop="headline" content="">
        <div class="page__inner-wrap">
          <section class="page__content" itemprop="text">
            
<p><span class="anchor" id="about-me"></span></p>

<p>I am a second-year PhD student in the Department of Computer Science at <a href="https://www.ucl.ac.uk/"><strong>University College London (UCL)</strong></a>, where I am fortunate to be co-supervised by <a href="https://heye.me/"><strong>Dr. He Ye</strong></a> and <a href="http://www0.cs.ucl.ac.uk/staff/F.Sarro/"><strong>Prof. Federica Sarro</strong></a>.
Previously, I completed my master’s degree at the School of Computer Science and Technology, <a href="https://www.hust.edu.cn"><strong>Huazhong University of Science and Technology (HUST)</strong></a>, advised by <a href="http://wanyao.me"><strong>Prof. Yao Wan</strong></a>.
My academic journey has also been enriched by collaborations with <a href="https://lingming.cs.illinois.edu/"><strong>Prof. Lingming Zhang</strong></a> at UIUC and <a href="https://sites.google.com/site/hongyujohn/"><strong>Prof. Hongyu Zhang</strong></a> at Chongqing University.</p>

<!--
I am also a co-founder of [**EuniAI**](https://euni.ai/), where we are building [**Prometheus**](https://github.com/EuniAI/Prometheus) — an open-source AI agent designed to push the boundaries of automated software development.
-->

<blockquote>
  <p>My research interests lie at the intersection of software engineering and artificial intelligence, with an emphasis on <strong>coding agents</strong>: how to build, evaluate, and make them reliable on real-world tasks.
I have published 10+ papers <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=HYu3DyEAAAAJ"><img src="https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/Zhaoyang-Chu/Zhaoyang-Chu.github.io@google-scholar-stats/gs_data_shieldsio.json&amp;logo=googlescholar&amp;logoColor=white&amp;style=for-the-badge&amp;color=4285F4" alt="Citations" style="vertical-align:middle;height:24px!important;width:auto" /></a> at top-tier international SE and AI conferences such as ICSE, FSE, ISSTA, ACL, EMNLP, ICML, and NAACL.
For more details about my academic background, please see my <a href="/assets/ZhaoyangChu_CV.pdf"><strong>CV</strong></a>.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>🤝 <strong>Let’s Connect</strong>: I am always eager to connect and collaborate, whether you share my interests or bring a different perspective from another field. If you’d like to discuss research, exchange ideas, or just say hi, feel free to reach out at <a href="mailto:zhaoyang.chu.25@ucl.ac.uk">zhaoyang.chu.25@ucl.ac.uk</a>, <a href="mailto:zychu418@gmail.com">zychu418@gmail.com</a>.</p>

<!--
🌟🌟 **Excited to share: I will be in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil for [ICSE 2026](https://conf.researchr.org/home/icse-2026) next April—looking forward to meeting many of you there!** 🤗🤗
-->

<!--
🌟🌟 **I will be in Vienna, Austria in September for ISSTA 2024! Hope to meet many of you there!** 🤗🤗
- **Code Intelligence**, e.g., code generation, code search, and vulnerability detection.
- **Trustworthy Artificial Intelligence**, e.g., explainability, privacy, and robustness.
-->

<h1 id="-news">🔥 News</h1>

<ul>
  <li><em>2026.10</em>:  🚀 Released <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.02459">OpenRUA</a>: off-the-shelf coding agents serve as zero-shot visuomotor policies through terminal access to ROS 2.</li>
  <li><em>2026.09</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.22535">TerminalWorld</a>, a benchmark of real-world terminal tasks reverse-engineered from in-the-wild terminal recordings, was accepted to <strong>NeurIPS 2026</strong>.</li>
  <li><em>2026.08</em>:  🤗 The <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/EuniAI/TerminalWorld">TerminalWorld dataset</a> exceeded <strong>20k downloads</strong> on Hugging Face!</li>
  <li><em>2026.06</em>:  🎙️ TerminalWorld was featured on <a href="https://lastweekin.ai/p/lwiai-podcast-246-gemini-35-omni">Last Week in AI</a> (ep. #246), a newsletter and podcast with 181k+ listeners.</li>
  <li><em>2026.05</em>:  🤗 The <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/EuniAI/TerminalWorld">TerminalWorld dataset</a> exceeded <strong>5,000 downloads</strong> on Hugging Face!</li>
  <li><em>2026.04</em>:  🎉 Two papers were accepted to <strong>ACL 2026</strong>: <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.11226">ExecVerify</a> on code execution reasoning and <a href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.findings-acl.434/">CGBridge</a> on structure-aware code understanding (Findings).</li>
  <li><em>2026.03</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3808139">Our paper</a> on hallucinations in LLM-based code summarization was accepted to <strong>FSE 2026</strong>.</li>
  <li><em>2025.09</em>:  🎓 Started my PhD at <strong>UCL</strong>, co-supervised by <a href="https://heye.me/">Dr. He Ye</a> and <a href="http://www0.cs.ucl.ac.uk/staff/F.Sarro/">Prof. Federica Sarro</a>.</li>
</ul>

<details>
  <summary style="cursor:pointer; color:#888; font-size:0.9em;">Show older news</summary>

  <ul>
    <li><em>2025.08</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.08343">NoWait</a>, which suppresses “Wait”-style self-reflection tokens for efficient reasoning, was accepted to <strong>EMNLP 2025</strong> Findings.</li>
    <li><em>2025.07</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.01333">CODERPE</a>, which uses role-player prompting to let LLMs evaluate code summaries, was accepted by <strong>IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering</strong>.</li>
    <li><em>2025.06</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13755">CodeEraser</a>, which erases sensitive memorization from code LLMs via machine unlearning, was accepted to <strong>ICSE 2026</strong>.</li>
    <li><em>2025.05</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.16645">CODESYNC</a>, on keeping LLMs in sync with evolving library APIs, was accepted to <strong>ICML 2025</strong>.</li>
    <li><em>2025.03</em>:  🏆 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.03783">Our SANER 2025 paper</a> received the <strong>IEEE TCSE Distinguished Paper Award</strong>!</li>
    <li><em>2025.01</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.04531">TESTEVAL</a>, a benchmark for test case generation with LLMs, was accepted to <strong>NAACL 2025</strong> Findings.</li>
    <li><em>2024.12</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.03783">Our study</a> on selecting pre-trained code models for reuse was accepted to <strong>SANER 2025</strong>.</li>
    <li><em>2024.03</em>:  🎉 <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.15687">CFExplainer</a>, a counterfactual explainer for GNN-based vulnerability detection, was accepted to <strong>ISSTA 2024</strong>.</li>
  </ul>

</details>

<!--
- *2022.09*: &nbsp;🎉 One paper was published in **Information Sciences**.
-->

